        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5182baaf-63e3-50ac-8967-43b5d3f508cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Singapore, North America, South Korea\n- Buildings: Tanjong Pagar Centre, One Raffles Place, UOB Plaza, Republic Plaza, 63 Building, Bank of China Tower\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, One Raffles Place was completed at 280 m tall.\n- In 1986, One Raffles Place became the tallest building in the world outside North America, surpassing South Korea's 63 Building, which had been completed one year earlier.\n- One Raffles Place later lost its status as the tallest building in the world outside North America to the Bank of China Tower.\n- For over 20 years, UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza jointly held the record for the tallest building in Singapore.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre is 290 m tall.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre is currently the tallest building in Singapore, breaking the long-held joint record of UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4b2fb342-ca46-5539-b5b5-e5cb4779afe5",
        "text": "Page: Tanjong Pagar Centre. Sentence: With a height of 290 m , it is currently the tallest building in Singapore, breaking the record held jointly by UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place and Republic Plaza for over 20 years.\nPage: One Raffles Place. Sentence: At 280 m , it was also the tallest building in the world outside North America at the time of its completion in 1986, surpassing South Korea's 63 Building completed one year earlier, until it was succeeded by the Bank of China Tower.",
